        "title": "docs: update site provider count to 58",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Update README, website metadata, all 23 site locales, the LLM index, and the social card to the canonical 58-provider count.\n- Derive the expected public count from `UsageProvider` during `make check` so future provider additions fail until every advertised surface is updated.\n- Bump both social-preview image URLs so crawlers fetch the regenerated card instead of serving the cached prior asset.\n- Preserve @kiranmagic7's regenerated 1200×630 social asset and contributor credit.\n\n## Validation\n- Exact head: `a99f3789cd62936491b27678dda97ef3f1b64b7d`.\n- `node Scripts/check-site-locales.mjs`: all locales and registry-derived provider counts pass.\n- `make check`: generated docs, locale checks, SwiftFormat, and SwiftLint clean.\n- Zero-retry full suite: 614/614 selections, 52/52 groups first-pass green, no retries, recoveries, or timeouts.\n- Autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings; 0.97 correctness confidence after fixing the social-image cache key.\n- Fresh local Chrome render of `docs/social.html`: 1200×630, “58 providers” visible, no clipping or layout regression; committed image independently inspected at the same dimensions.\n\n## Risk\nLow. Runtime app behavior is unchanged. The new lint guard follows the repository's one-case-per-line `UsageProvider` enum style and intentionally fails when public count surfaces drift.\n\n## Dependencies\nNo dependency changes; freshness review not applicable.\n",
